    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d571-a1">

                <pb facs="0894" n="766" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg766"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 10.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Messrs. Alexandre &amp; Sons to Mr.
                    Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >New York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-11-28"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 28,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: We beg to advise your Department that the
                    Spanish consul continues to exact a duty of 10 cents per 1,000 kilos (2,200
                    pounds) as tonnage dues on cargo shipped by our steamers to Havana, which we
                    were led to think was contrary to intention of the late treaty made between
                    United States and Spain, and so have continued paying same under protest.</p>
                <p>Can we not hope that this may be stopped?</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer>F. ALEXANDRE &amp; SONS.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
